# Downloaded and derived data is not committed. Everything under data/ is
# rebuilt by scripts/01_build_data.py, it runs to about 350 MB, and several
# sources do not permit redistribution. The per-source position is recorded in
# references/source_register.csv.
#
# The leading slash is load-bearing. A bare `data/` pattern matches a directory
# of that name at ANY depth, which silently excluded the whole of
# src/minvol/data/ (universe, prices, fundamentals, splits, market cap and the
# rest) from a commit and would have published a repository that cannot run.
# Anchoring the pattern to the repository root is what restricts it to the real
# data directory.
/data/

# Run logs, same anchoring for the same reason.
/logs/

# No negated exceptions here either. A `!/data/raw/.gitkeep` style rule forces
# git to walk into the directory and stat all 1,282 files to work out what the
# exception matches, which turns `git add` into a minutes-long operation over a
# network mount. Paths.ensure() recreates the directories on first run, so no
# placeholder files are needed.

# Figures and tables ARE committed. They are under a megabyte together, the
# report embeds the figures directly, and a reader browsing the repository
# should see the results without running the pipeline first.

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.venv/
venv/
.env

.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
